From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@visma.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:31:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] stubs: weak symbols with the Tiny C Compiler too

stubs.h makes the stub definitions (serverGeneration, ErrorF, the font
client hooks) weak only under GCC 3 and later on ELF, so that an X server
linking the library statically overrides them.  tcc generates ELF, supports
__attribute__((weak)), and defines neither __GNUC__ nor __ELF__; without
the attribute a static link of a server against libXfont.a fails with
'serverGeneration' defined twice.  Accept __TINYC__ as well.
---
 src/stubs/stubs.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/stubs/stubs.h b/src/stubs/stubs.h
index 9e71806..c86d5f8 100644
--- a/src/stubs/stubs.h
+++ b/src/stubs/stubs.h
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
 #endif
 
 /* this probably works for Mach-O too, but probably not for PE */
-#if defined(__ELF__) && defined(__GNUC__) && (__GNUC__ >= 3)
+#if (defined(__ELF__) && defined(__GNUC__) && (__GNUC__ >= 3)) || defined(__TINYC__)
 #define weak __attribute__((weak))
 #else
 #define weak
